	<field name="span_type"                       offset="0x4.0"    size="0x0.4" access="RW" enum="LOCAL_ETH=0x0,REMOTE_ETH=0x1,REMOTE_ETH_L2=0x2,REMOTE_ETH_L3=0x3,LOCAL_IB=0x4,REMOTE_IB_LOCAL_UD=0xa,REMOTE_IB_GLOBAL_UD=0xb" descr="See Span Types0x0: LOCAL_ETH0x1: REMOTE_ETH0x2: REMOTE_ETH_L20x3: REMOTE_ETH_L30x4: LOCAL_IB0xA: REMOTE_IB_LOCAL_UD0xB: REMOTE_IB_GLOBAL_UD" />
	<field name="trim"                            offset="0x4.4"    size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="Trimming agent enable.When enabled, the agent is used for trimming only. Agent can’t be used\;for mirroring at any trigger point.Supported only with INGRESS_SHARED_BUFFER trigger.Supported from Spectrum-5 onwards.Supported for pa_id=0 only." />
	<field name="imp"                             offset="0x4.16"   size="0x0.1" access="OP" descr="Is Multi Port:0: Mirror only to one port - according to system_port description1: Mirror to one of the multi_ports, see nmp descriptionIf nmp ≠ 0, the decision to which port to mirror will be according to\;multi_port[ingress_port_lag_hash[1:0]]" />
	<field name="nmp"                             offset="0x4.17"   size="0x0.2" access="OP" descr="Number of Multi Port:0: mirror to single port, multi_port[0]1: mirror to one of 2 ports, multi_port[0] and multi_port[1]2: mirror to one of 4 ports, multi_port[0] - multi_port[3]Reserved when imp = 0." />
	<field name="tr"                              offset="0x4.24"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="Truncate. Indicates all packets mirrored to this Analyzer port will be\;truncated.Truncation size is defined by truncation_sizeFor Spectrum, packets from CPU to a truncation-enabled agent will not be\;mirrored. For Spectrum-2, packets from CPU to a truncation-enabled agent will be\;mirroredReserved when system_port is to CPUReserved when MPAT.itc = 1" />
	<field name="be"                              offset="0x4.25"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" enum="NOT_DISCARD=0x0,DISCARD=0x1" descr="Best Effort. Indicates mirroring traffic should not cause packet drop or\;back pressure but will discard the mirroring packets. Mirroring packets\;will be forwarded in a best effort manner.0: NOT_DISCARD - Do not discard mirrored packets1: DISCARD - Discard mirrored packets if causing congestionRelevant both for ingress mirror and egress mirror" />
	<field name="qos"                             offset="0x4.26"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" enum="CONFIGURED=0x0,MAINTAIN=0x1" descr="Quality of Service mode0: CONFIGURED - QoS parameters (Switch Priority, and encapsulation\;PCP, DEI, DSCP or VL) are configured1: MAINTAIN - QoS parameters (Switch Priority, Color) are the same as\;in the original packet that has triggered the mirroring. For SPAN\;also the pcp,dei are maintained. Reserved when Spectrum.For SPAN packets the PCP, DEI is as mirrored packet" />
	<field name="c"                               offset="0x4.28"   size="0x0.1" access="OP" descr="Clear countersClears the buffer_drop and be_dropcounters" />
	<field name="e"                               offset="0x4.31"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="Enable. Indicating the Port Analyzer is enabledNote: before disabling a port analyzer, software should make sure no\;port / rule is associated with the Port Analyzer to be disabled." />
	<field name="truncation_size"                 offset="0x8.0"    size="0x0.13" access="RW" descr="Truncation Size.Sets the truncation size in case truncation is enabled.Unit is 1 byte.Granularity is 4 bytes.For Spectrum-1: minimum value is 32BFor Quantum and Spectrum-2/3: minimum value is 48BFrom Spectrum-4: minimum value is 64B.\;Reserved when span_type is LOCALIBReserved when MPAT.itc = 1" />
	<field name="switch_prio"                     offset="0x8.16"   size="0x0.4" access="RW" descr="Switch Prio for the mirrored/trimmed packet.In mirroring:Reserved when imp=0.Reserved when qos=1 (MAINTAIN).Reserved for IB-switch.In trimming used when trim_qos=0, reserved otherwise." />
	<field name="tclass"                          offset="0x8.24"   size="0x0.4" access="RW" descr="Traffic class of the mirrored/trimmed packet.Reserved when the mirror port is CPU port (it is set by\;HTGT.cpu_tclass).In mirroring:Reserved when imp=0Reserved when qos=1 (MAINTAIN).Reserved for IB-switch.In trimming used when trim_qos=0, reserved otherwise." />
	<field name="itc"                             offset="0x8.31"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="Ignore Truncation Configuration0: use MPAT.tr and MPAT.truncation_size to configure truncation profile.1: use ITPR to configure truncation profile. See\;ITPR - Infrastructure Truncation Profile Register Fields.Valid for Spectrum-4 and on." />
	<field name="pid"                             offset="0xc.0"    size="0x0.14" access="RW" descr="Policer IDRange is MOGCR.mirroring_pid_base..\;(MOGCR.mirroring_pid_base +\;cap_max_span_analyzers - 1).Accurate policers are supported within this range. An accurate\;policer must use an even PID and consumes the following odd-numbered\;PID.Architecture note: Do not enlarge this range for Spectrum-4 and\;Spectrum-5. Keeping the existing SPAN policers in the lower half of\;the potential 16-entry range is required for the future policer\;relocation flow. Allowing allocation in the upper half would make\;that relocation impossible. The enlarged range can be supported\;from Spectrum-6, where no migration from the legacy mapping is\;required.See pid in QPCR,\;section 14.12.7 - QPCR - QoS Policer Configuration RegisterNote: the policer takes packet length prior to truncation. The policer\;must have color_aware=not, type=srDCM, violate_action=discard.Reserved when Spectrum-1 and Quantum/-2." />
	<field name="pide"                            offset="0xc.15"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="Policer enableFor more details about policers, refer to\;section 13.7.5 - PolicerNote: for mirror to CPU: MPAT.pid is enabled then the trap-group-policer\;will not policeReserved when Spectrum-1 and Quantum/-2." />
	<field name="encapsulation"                   offset="0x10.0"   size="0x50.0" subnode="mpat_reg_encapsulation_auto_ext" access="RW" union_selector="$(parent).span_type" descr="Remote SPAN encapsulation. The encapsulation information is based on the\;span_type field. The following tables provide a reference to the\;encapsulation fields for the different SPAN types:Local SPAN Layout.Remote SPAN Ethernet VLAN Layout.Encapsulated Remote SPAN Ethernet L2 Layout.Encapsulated Remote SPAN Ethernet L3 Layout.Local SPAN InfiniBand Layout.Remote SPAN InfiniBand Local UD Layout.Remote SPAN InfiniBand Global UD Layout." />
	<field name="buffer_drop_high"                offset="0x60.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RO" descr="Counter:Number of packet drops on the analyzer agent due to buffer sizeReserved when Quantum switches." />
	<field name="buffer_drop_low"                 offset="0x64.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RO" descr="Counter:Number of packet drops on the analyzer agent due to buffer sizeReserved when Quantum switches." />
	<field name="be_drop_high"                    offset="0x68.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RO" descr="Counter:Number of packet drops on the analyzer agent due to Best Effort when be\;is enabledReserved when Quantum switches." />
	<field name="be_drop_low"                     offset="0x6c.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RO" descr="Counter:Number of packet drops on the analyzer agent due to Best Effort when be\;is enabledReserved when Quantum switches." />
	<field name="pc"                              offset="0x78.0"   size="0x0.2" access="RW" enum="No_padding=0x0,TwoBytes_padding=0x1" descr="Pad Count0: No_padding1: TwoBytes_paddingSupported from Spectrum-4 and above." />
	<field name="multi_port"                      offset="0x7c.16"  size="0x8.0" access="RW" high_bound="3" low_bound="0" descr="System port.If nmp ≠ 0, CPU port cannot be used.If (mngr_type == “Hypervisor”)Unique port identifier for the final destination of the packetIf (mngr_type == “Local Network Manager”) and the port from which the\;command came from is Ethernet:Local PortWhen CPU port:span_type must be LOCAL_ETH or LOCAL_IBtr is reserved (no truncation)" />
	<field name="trim_fwd_profile"                offset="0x8c.0"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="Trim And Forward (T&amp;F) trimming profile selector.Profile has to be of type=FWD, see\;section 7.17.1 - MOTPR - Monitoring Trimming Profile Register.Supported from Spectrum-5." />
	<field name="trim_bts_profile"                offset="0x8c.8"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="[Spectrum-6]Back To Sender (BTS) trimming profile selector.Profile has to be of type=BTS, see\;section 7.17.1 - MOTPR - Monitoring Trimming Profile Register.Supported from Spectrum-6." />
	<field name="ip_len_fix"                      offset="0x8c.16"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="[Spectrum-6]IP length fix for trimmed packets.When enabled, IP length field is fixed after truncation.0: No change (default)1: Update IP length field after truncation.Reserved when itc=1.Supported from Spectrum-6." />
	<field name="trim_qos"                        offset="0x8c.20"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" enum="AGENT=0x0,MAPPED=0x1" descr="[Spectrum-6]Quality of Service trimming mode.0: AGENT - take trimming Switch Priority and Traffic Class from the\;trimming agent (MPAT).1: MAPPED - map trimming Switch Priority and Traffic Class from\;original Switch Priority (MOTSPT).Supported from Spectrum-6." />
	<field name="pcp_rw"                          offset="0x90.0"   size="0x0.2" access="RW" enum="PRESERVE=0x0,CLEAR=0x2,SET=0x3" descr="Rewrite PCP and DEI according to the Switch Prio set by the agent.0: PRESERVE - preserves pcp_rewrite_en2: CLEAR - clears pcp_rewrite_en3: SET - sets pcp_rewrite_enSupported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0." />
	<field name="dscp_rw"                         offset="0x90.8"   size="0x0.2" access="RW" enum="PRESERVE=0x0,CLEAR=0x2,SET=0x3" descr="Rewrite DSCP according to the Switch Prio set by the agent.0: PRESERVE - preserves dscp_rewrite_en2: CLEAR - clears dscp_rewrite_en3: SET - sets dscp_rewrite_enSupported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0." />
	<field name="dscp"                            offset="0x90.16"  size="0x0.6" access="RW" descr="The DSCP value to overwrite with.Supported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0." />
	<field name="overwrite_dscp"                  offset="0x90.23"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="Whether to overwrite DSCP with dscp provided by the trimming agent.Note: Can be overridden by dscp_rewrite_en if set.Supported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0." />
	<field name="ignore_agent_trim_profile"       offset="0x90.31"  size="0x0.1" access="OP" descr="Ignores MPAT trimming profile fields.Supported on Write and on Query.Trimming profile can be set in MOTPR. See\;section 7.17.1 - MOTPR - Monitoring Trimming Profile Register.Supported in Spectrum-5 only." />
	<field name="emt_index"                       offset="0x98.0"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="Egress Modifier Template binding 0.EMT index.Range: 0 .. cap_max_emts - 1.See FMTC, FMTE.Supported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0 or when emt_bind = NOP." />
	<field name="emt_bind"                        offset="0x98.8"   size="0x0.4" access="RW" enum="NOP=0x0,PUSH=0x1,EDIT=0x2,POP=0x4" descr="Egress Modifier Template binding 0.Bind an EMT:0: NOP - no bind1: PUSH - bind as push2: EDIT - bind as edit4: POP - bind as popSupported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0." />
	<field name="modifier_base"                   offset="0x98.16"  size="0x0.4" access="RW" descr="Egress Modifier Template binding 0.Modifier Base Label.Push/Edit/Pop will be applied in the beginning of the following selected\;field of encapsulated header:Note: Pop is allowed only with SOP (0).0: SOP (start of packet)1: New MAC header2: New ETHERTYPE 3: New IPv4/IPv6 header4: New MPLS 5: New VxLAN/Geneve/VxLAN-GPE/NVGRE 6: New GRE header7: New UDP header8: New Flex Encap 9: New Inner MAC header 11: New Inner ETHER Type Supported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0 or when emt_bind = NOP." />
	<field name="modifier_offset"                 offset="0x98.24"  size="0x0.2" access="RW" enum="ZERO=0x0,CBSET_0=0x1,CBSET_1=0x2" descr="Egress Modifier Template binding 0.Offset on top of modifier_base.0: ZERO - zero offset1: CBSET_0 - offset is custom_bytes[1:0]2: CBSET_1 - offset is custom_bytes[3:2]Supported in Spectrum-5 only.Reserved when trim=0 or when emt_bind = NOP." />
</node>

