	<field name="max_shaper_rate"                 offset="0x10.0"   size="0x0.31" access="RW" descr="Max shaper information rateFor all hierarchies at a non-CPU port, and for port-hierarchy on CPU\;ports:bps mode, Units of 1000bpsGranularity is 200mbpsError is up to 3% from configuration (for example, when rate is\;configured to 200mbps, the actual rate may be 206mbps)Reading reveals the actual rate (e.g., 206 in the above example)On get, actual values are returned which might differ from the set\;valuesWhen mase is 1, value 0 enables the max shaper and blocks all\;traffic. For non-CPU ports, the maximum effective shaper rate\;corresponds to the maximum port speed supported by the ASIC. This\;limit is not adjusted for the configured port width or speed, and the\;actual traffic rate cannot exceed the port’s line rate.In bps mode for CPU ports, the maximum effective shaper rate is\;greater than the maximum bandwidth supported by each CPU-port\;destination path. This limit is not adjusted for the negotiated PCIe\;link width or speed, and the actual rate of host-bound traffic cannot\;exceed the usable PCIe bandwidth.For Tclass and [DWIP] Sub Group hierarchies of CPU ports:bps mode:Units of 1000bpsInput granularity is 1000bps. The device rounds the configured\;value to the closest supported rate; therefore, the effective\;hardware rate step is not fixedError is up to 1% from configurationpacket per sec mode:Units of 1 packet per secInput granularity is 10 packets per sec on Spectrum and 1 packet\;per sec from Spectrum-2. The device rounds the\;configured value to the closest supported rate; therefore, the\;effective hardware rate step is not fixedError is up to 1% from configurationFrom Spectrum-2, the maximum effective shaper rate in packet per\;sec mode is greater than the maximum rate supported by the CPU-port\;destination paths, even for minimum-size Ethernet frames. The actual\;host-bound traffic rate cannot exceed the usable PCIe bandwidth.Note: For rates lower than 10Kbps or lower than 100 packets per\;sec, error is up to 10%.On get, the device returns the actual integer rate, which might\;differ from the configured value.Reserved when ptps = 1Reserved when element_hierarchy is 1Value of 0x7FFF_FFFF means “all allowed” or “shaper disabled”. Values\;above the maximum rate report disabled as well." />
	<field name="mase"                            offset="0x10.31"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" enum="disable=0x0,enable=0x1" descr="Max shaper configuration enable. Enables configuration of\;max_shaper_rate, max_shaper_bs on this ETS element.0: disable1: enableReserved when element_hierarchy is 1" />
	<field name="dwrr_weight"                     offset="0x18.0"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="DWRR weight on the link going down from the ETS element:The percentage of bandwidth guaranteed to a ETS within its hierarchy.The sum of dwrr_weight values across all ETS elements within one\;hierarchy should equal 100.This field is reserved when dwrr is set to strict priority.For switches only:A single ETS element weight range is 0..100. The sum of dwrr_weight\;values across all ETS elements within one hierarchy can exceed 100.See limitations in\;qos/advanced_packet_scheduling:Deficit Weighted Round Robin (DWRR)." />
	<field name="dwrr"                            offset="0x18.15"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="DWRR or strict priority on the link going down from the ETS element:0: strict priority - default from Spectrum-41: DWRRFor Spectrum-1, Spectrum-2 and Spectrum-3 DWRR with weights of 0 is\;configured by default, which result in a round robin arbitration.Reserved for Quantum switches." />
	<field name="de"                              offset="0x18.31"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="DWRR configuration enable. Enables configuration of the dwrr and\;dwrr_weight.0: disable1: enableReserved for QM switches." />
	<field name="max_shaper_bs"                   offset="0x1c.0"   size="0x0.6" access="RW" descr="Max shaper Burst size.On bytes mode (pb=0) burst size is 512•2max_shaper_bs [bits].On packet mode (pb=1) burst size is 2max_shaper_bs [packets].For Spectrum: Range is: 5..25.For Spectrum-2 onwards: Range is: 11..25.Value of 0 is configured as minimum when shaper is enabled.Reserved when ptps = 1." />
	<field name="min_shaper_bs"                   offset="0x1c.16"  size="0x0.6" access="RW" descr="Min shaper Burst size.On bytes mode (pb=0) burst size is 512•2min_shaper_bs [bits].On packet mode (pb=1) burst size is 2min_shaper_bs [packets].For Spectrum: Range is: 5..25.For Spectrum-2 onwards: Range is: 11..25.Value of 0 is configured as minimum when shaper is enabled.Reserved when ptps = 1.Reserved for QM switches." />
