<node name="qpcr_ext"                             size="0x28.0" descr="" >
	<field name="pid"                             offset="0x0.0"    size="0x0.14" access="INDEX" descr="Policer ID.Global policers are numbered from 0 to cap_max_policers_global - 1.Per-port policers are numbered from 0 to cap_max_policers_per_port - 1.Storm policers are numbered from 0 to\;cap_max_policers_storm_control - 1.For Spectrum switches, an accurate policer or a dual rate policer uses\;the selected even-numbered PID and the following odd-numbered PID.\;Software must not allocate the following PID to another policer." />
	<field name="g"                               offset="0x0.14"   size="0x0.2" access="INDEX" enum="POLICER_GLOBAL=0x2,POLICER_STORM=0x3" descr="2: POLICER_GLOBAL - global policer configuration3: POLICER_STORM - storm control policer configurationFor IB switches, g must be POLICER_GLOBAL." />
	<field name="type"                            offset="0x4.8"    size="0x0.2" access="RW" descr="policer type:0: srTCM, single rate three colors marking. This mode is not supported\;by Spectrum switches1: srDCM, single rate dual colors marking.2: trTCM, dual rate three colors marking. Reserved when\;is_acc=1.Editing of this field is not allowed for a bounded policer.IB switches support only srDCM." />
	<field name="ir_units"                        offset="0x4.12"   size="0x0.1" access="OP" descr="0: cir and eir use units of 10^6 bits/sec (Mbps)1: cir and eir use units of 10^3 bits/sec (Kbps)Reserved when IB switches." />
	<field name="is_acc"                          offset="0x4.13"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" enum="STATISTICAL=0x0,ACCURATE=0x1" descr="[DWIP] Policer accuracy mode.0: STATISTICAL - The policer uses statistical updates (default).1: ACCURATE - The policer is updated for every metered packet.Editing of this field is not allowed for a bounded policer.Reserved for storm control policers (g=3).Reserved for IB switches.Supported from Spectrum-4." />
	<field name="bytes"                           offset="0x4.14"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="0: meter based on packets/sec1: meter based on bytes/secThis field is reserved when mode=1 (packet sampling).Editing of this field is not allowed for a bounded policer.Reserved when IB switches (support only packets/sec)." />
	<field name="color_aware"                     offset="0x4.15"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="0: meter is not color aware1: meter is color awareEditing of this field is not allowed for a bounded policerReserved when storm control policers.Reserved when IB switches." />
	<field name="add_counter"                     offset="0x4.30"   size="0x0.1" access="OP" descr="Add a value to the counters. The value of violate_count is added to\;the counter for the selected pid.Reserved when IB switches." />
	<field name="clear_counter"                   offset="0x4.31"   size="0x0.1" access="OP" descr="Clear counters. Setting clear_counter resets violate_count for\;the selected pid.Reserved when IB switches." />
	<field name="ebs"                             offset="0x8.16"   size="0x0.6" access="RW" descr="Excessive burst sizeOn packet metering (bytes=0), the burst size is 2^ebs packets.On byte metering (bytes=1), the burst size is 512 * 2^ebs bits.In Spectrum switches, value 0 is used for dropping all traffic.Spectrum-1 when bits mode: Range is 4..25.Spectrum-1 when packet mode: Range is 4..24.Spectrum-2 and on when bits mode: Range is 4..31.Spectrum-2 and on when packet mode: Range is 4..26.On Spectrum-2 and on, packet mode, with a minimum ebs of 8, there will\;be no more than 3% errors (drops/sent packets) in 95% of the cases.Reserved when type is srDCM or is_acc=1." />
	<field name="cbs"                             offset="0x8.24"   size="0x0.6" access="RW" descr="Committed burst size.On packet metering (bytes=0), the burst size is 2^cbs packets.On byte metering (bytes=1), the burst size is 512 * 2^cbs bits.In Spectrum switches, value 0 is used for dropping all traffic.Spectrum-1 when bits mode: Range is 4..25.Spectrum-1 when packet mode: Range is 4..24.Spectrum-2 and on when bits mode: Range is 4..31.Spectrum-2 and on when packet mode: Range is 4..26.On Spectrum-2 and on, in packet mode with a minimum cbs of 8, no more\;than 3% of packets will be dropped (errors/drops per sent packet) in 95%\;of cases.Note: With small cir rates (up to 50Mbps), the policer might limit the\;bandwidth further when cbs is smaller than 6.Quantum: Range is 4..11 (16..2K Packets/Sec)." />
	<field name="cir"                             offset="0xc.0"    size="0x4.0" access="RW" descr="Committed information rate.For Spectrum switches: resolution error is up to 1%. Reading will\;provide the exact value used by the HW.On byte metering (bytes=1), the units are selected by ir_units.On packet metering (bytes=0), cir is in packets/sec.Spectrum-1 has max 2Tbps or max 2Gpps.Spectrum-2 and on has max 6.4Tbps or max 9.5Gpps.Note: With small cir rates (up to 50Mbps), the policer might limit the\;bandwidth further when cbs is smaller than 6.Quantum: range: 64..100,000 packets/sec. HW rounds to N * 64.\;Resolution error is up to 1%." />
	<field name="eir"                             offset="0x10.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RW" descr="Excess information rate.For Spectrum switches: resolution error is up to 1%. Reading will\;provide the exact value used by the HW.On byte metering (bytes=1), the units are selected by ir_units.On packet metering (bytes=0), eir is in packets/sec.Spectrum-1 has max 2Tbps or max 2Gpps.Spectrum-2 and on has max 6.4Tbps or max 9.5Gpps.Reserved when type is srDCM or is_acc=1." />
	<field name="exceed_action"                   offset="0x14.0"   size="0x0.4" access="RW" enum="forward=0x0,discard=0x1,forward_and_set_color_to_yellow=0x2" descr="Action for packets classified yellow by the policer (packets that exceed\;cbs but do not exceed ebs):0: forward - Not supported by Spectrum switches.1: discard - Not supported by Spectrum switches.2: forward_and_set_color_to_yellowEditing of this field is not allowed for a bounded policer.Reserved when type is srDCM or is_acc=1." />
	<field name="violate_action"                  offset="0x18.0"   size="0x0.4" access="RW" enum="forward=0x0,discard=0x1,forward_and_set_color_to_red=0x2,reset_trap_prio_to_0=0x3" descr="Action for packets classified Red by the policer (e.g. packets that\;exceed cbs when type is srDCM or exceed ebs when type is\;trTCM):0: forward - Not supported by Spectrum switches.1: discard2: forward_and_set_color_to_red3: reset_trap_prio_to_0 - This option disable the trap, supported\;from Spectrum-4.For Spectrum switches, storm control policers’ action must be\;discard.Editing of this field is not allowed for a bounded policer.IB switches support only discard" />
	<field name="violate_count_high"              offset="0x20.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RW" descr="Counts the number of times violate_action occurred for this pid.Reserved when IB switches." />
