	<field name="nve_ttl_mc"                      offset="0x8.0"    size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="The TTL for NVE Tunnel encapsulation of underlay multicast packets." />
	<field name="nve_fl_suffix"                   offset="0xc.0"    size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="NVE Flow Label SuffixFor NVE Tunnel encapsulation: Flow Label SuffixFor Tunnel encapsulation the 8 least significant bits are calculated as\;follow:enc_flh=0: 8 lsb = enc_fl_suffixenc_flh=1: 8 lsb = enc_fl_suffix | hash [7:0] (bitwise OR)Reserved when nve_flh = 1*** Note: this field is not supported by current FW, the value is\;always ‘0’ ***Supported from Spectrum-2" />
	<field name="nve_fl_prefix"                   offset="0xc.8"    size="0x0.12" access="RW" descr="NVE Flow Label PrefixFor NVE Tunnel encapsulation: Constant 12 most significant bits of the\;flow label.Spectrum: reserved when nve_flh = 0Spectrum-2: not reserved" />
	<field name="nve_flh"                         offset="0xc.24"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="NVE Flow Label HashFor NVE Tunnel encapsulation:0: Flow Label is static- Spectrum-1: ‘0’- Spectrum-2 and on: by {nve_fl_prefix, nve_fl_suffix}1: Flow Label 8 least significant bits are calculated from ECMP hash\;bitwise OR with enc_fl_suffix, and 12msb are configured by nve_fl_prefixSee\;section 16.14.6 - RECR - Router ECMP Configuration Register,\;section 16.14.7 - RECR_V2 - Router ECMP Configuration Version 2 Register" />
	<field name="nve_flc"                         offset="0xc.25"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="For NVE Tunnel encapsulation: Flow Label Copy from inner0: Calculate flow label using nve_flh.1: If packet is IPv6 and encapsulation is IPv6, copy the whole flow\;label from the packet header. Otherwise, calculate flow label using\;nve_flh." />
	<field name="nve_udp_sport_suffix"            offset="0x10.0"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="NVE UDP Source Port SuffixWhen NVE encap - the 8 least significant bits of NVE UDP source port are\;calculated as follow:nve_udp_sport_type=0: 8 lsb = nve_udp_sport_suffixnve_udp_sport_type=1: 8 lsb = nve_udp_sport_suffix | hash [7:0]\;(bitwise OR)For Spectrum: the 8 least significant bits are set by LAG hashSee\;section 9.17.5 - SLCR_V2 - Switch LAG Configuration 2 Register,\;section 9.17.5 - SLCR_V2 - Switch LAG Configuration 2 Register.For Spectrum-2: the 8 least significant bits are set by ECMP hash, see\;section 16.14.6 - RECR - Router ECMP Configuration Register,\;section 16.14.7 - RECR_V2 - Router ECMP Configuration Version 2 RegisterReserved when NVE Tunnel encapsulation is NVGRE" />
	<field name="nve_udp_sport_prefix"            offset="0x10.8"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="NVE UDP Source Port PrefixWhen NVE encap - constant 8 most significant bits of the NVE UDP source\;port.Reserved when NVE Tunnel encapsulation is NVGRE" />
	<field name="et_vlan"                         offset="0x10.20"  size="0x0.2" access="RW" descr="EtherType used for when VLAN is pushed at decap0: ether_type0 (default)1: ether_type12: ether_type2 Ethertype IDs are configured by SVER, see\;section 9.13.1 - SVER - Switch VLAN EtherType RegisterReserved when Spectrum-2, see SPVID" />
	<field name="nve_udp_sport_type"              offset="0x10.24"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="NVE UDP source port typeFor NVE Tunnel encapsulation (VXLAN, VXLAN-GPE or GENEVE):0: Source UDP is fixed - 8 msb are nve_src_udp_port_prefix, 8 lsb are:\;Spectrum-1 ‘0’, Spectrum-2 and on: nve_udp_sport_suffix1: Source UDP 8 least significant bits are calculated from hash and\;nve_udp_sport_suffix (see description of nve_udp_sport_suffix), and 8msb\;are configured by nve_src_udp_port_prefixFor NVE Tunnel encapsulation (NVGRE):0: NVGRE.flow_id is ‘0’1: NVGRE.flow_id (8 bits) is set by hash" />
	<field name="nve_enc_orig_we"                 offset="0x10.30"  size="0x0.1" access="WO" descr="Write enable to nve_enc_origReserved when Spectrum-2" />
	<field name="nve_enc_orig"                    offset="0x10.31"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="VLAN handling of overlay packet at encap:0: STRIP_TAG - 1 VLAN tag is stripped (if existed at ingress) (default)1: KEEP_ORIG - all VLAN tags of original packet are keptWhen overlay router and KEEP_ORIG the inner vid is 0Reserved when Spectrum-2, see SPVTR.epvid_mode" />
	<field name="nve_group_size_mc"               offset="0x18.0"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="For NVE Tunnel multicast:The amount of sequential link lists of MC entries. The first link list\;is configured by SFD.underlay_mc_ptrValid ranges:1, 2, 4, 8 16, 32, 64The link lists are configured by TNUMTThe hash is set by LAG hashSee\;section 18.11.6 - TNUMT - Tunneling NVE Underlay Multicast Table RegisterSee\;section 9.17.5 - SLCR_V2 - Switch LAG Configuration 2 Register,\;section 9.17.5 - SLCR_V2 - Switch LAG Configuration 2 Register.Reserved when Spectrum-2 and on" />
	<field name="nve_group_size_flood"            offset="0x1c.0"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="For NVE Tunnel flooding or BC:The amount of sequential link lists of flooding or BC entries. The first\;link list is configured by SFMR.nve_tunnel_flood_ptrValid ranges:1, 2, 4, 8 16, 32, 64The link lists are configured by TNUMTThe hash is set by LAG hashSee\;section 18.11.6 - TNUMT - Tunneling NVE Underlay Multicast Table RegisterSee\;section 9.17.5 - SLCR_V2 - Switch LAG Configuration 2 Register,\;section 9.17.5 - SLCR_V2 - Switch LAG Configuration 2 Register.Reserved when Spectrum-2 and on" />
	<field name="underlay_virtual_router"         offset="0x20.0"   size="0x0.16" access="RW" descr="Underlay virtual routerReserved when Spectrum-2" />
	<field name="dis_nve_opt_chk"                 offset="0x20.24"  size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="Spectrum-1/2/3 only.Disable DISCARD_DEC_NVE_OPTIONS only for reserved bits:0: Enable check for reserved bits1: Disable check for reserved bitsDefault value is 0.E.g when packet with reserved bits ≠ 0 should not be dropped this field\;should be set to 1." />
